### Update default payment method

To update a customer's default payment method, get that payment method's[`token`](/braintree/docs/reference/response/payment-method/node#token)and pass it as the`default_payment_method_token`value below:### Callback
```javascript

braintree.customer.update("theCustomerId", {
  defaultPaymentMethodToken: "theToken",
}, (err, result) => {
});

```

### Promise
```javascript

braintree.customer.update("theCustomerId", {
  defaultPaymentMethodToken: "theToken",
}).then(result => { });

```


### Card verification

By default we will run[credit card validations](/braintree/docs/reference/general/validation-errors/all#credit-card)but not perform[verification](/braintree/docs/guides/credit-cards/server-side/node#card-verification). Braintree strongly recommends verifying all cards before they are stored in your Vault by[enabling card verification for your entire account](/braintree/articles/control-panel/vault/card-verification)in the Control Panel. If you choose to manually verify cards, set`verify_card`to`true`.### Callback
```javascript

braintree.customer.update("theCustomerId", {
  paymentMethodNonce: nonceFromTheClient,
  creditCard: {
    options: {
      updateExistingToken: "theToken",
      verifyCard: true
    }
  }
}, (err, result) => {
});

```

### Promise
```javascript

braintree.customer.update("theCustomerId", {
  paymentMethodNonce: nonceFromTheClient,
  creditCard: {
    options: {
      updateExistingToken: "theToken",
      verifyCard: true
    }
  }
}).then(result => { });

```

**IMPORTANT**
If you are using our Premium Fraud Management Tools, we strongly recommend passing[`device_data`](/braintree/docs/guides/premium-fraud-management-tools/server-side/node#using-device-data)each time you verify a card.
